section: ghc-internal
synopsis: Avoid unnecessary allocations in bignum division in the Haskell (native) backend
issues: #27231
mrs: !15998
description:
    The long-division loop of the Haskell (native) bignum backend now
    subtracts the partial product in place, so ``bigNatQuotRem#``,
    ``bigNatQuot`` and ``bigNatRem`` no longer allocate a temporary BigNat
    per quotient word.
